WEBVTT

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.060
Open!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.500
Hanna-chan? What's wrong?

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.460
Question. Suzuko-san,

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.130
have you heard any rumors 
about Selector battles?

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.450
No.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.410
Acknowledgment.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.250
Why? Did something happen?

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.550
Denial. Nothing in particular.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.820
Remember what Mizushima-san said?

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.820
That the battles would begin again.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.440
So I'm gathering information, just in case.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.080
But...

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.770
Understanding. Don't worry.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.820
I don't want to get involved 
in the battles myself.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.800
Oh, Hanna-sama,

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.530
you're not going to tell her you 
were chosen as a Selector?

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.790
Foolishness.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.080
Suzuko-san seems to have not been chosen,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.290
so there's no need to tell her.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.730
You're so kind.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.240
Request.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.660
Actually, there's something 
I wanted to ask you.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.630
Give me more details about these battles.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.930
I don't know any more than 
I told you yesterday.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:44.030
Wait...

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.200
Perhaps I did know something else...

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.770
But I forgot.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.040
You're going to rip me up?

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.630
Stop! Don't stop!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.020
Hanna-sama, when I didn't tell 
you about your brother,

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.060
you didn't do anything to me.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:06.010
You may punish me now by 
torturing me, if you wish.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:06.920
Refusal.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.600
That was a necessary experience for me.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.700
So in a sense, I'm grateful 
to you, Anonymous-chan.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:15.440
You are?

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.710
What a shame.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.600
Hitoe's out with a cold today.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.130
I got a text.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.340
Ruuko? Ruuko!

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.850
Sorry...

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.080
What did you say?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.050
If you want to talk to someone, 
I'm always here for you.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.690
Yuzuki...

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.570
The Selector battles are still continuing?

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.790
Yes, that's what a girl 
named Mizushima-san said.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.570
But you stopped them, didn't you?

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.760
But she says they're not over.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.540
No...

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:58.800
So she asked me to help her end them for real...

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.200
Umph!

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.250
But I told her no.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.140
Was that really the right thing to do, though?

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.180
It was.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.040
You did enough last time.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:13.810
It's not your problem anymore.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:16.340
Yeah...

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.050
Hitoe, are you okay?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.570
I'm fine, Midoriko.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.200
Oh! Midori-san!

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.420
Midoriko is fine.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.630
I'm sorry, I wasn't thinking.

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.460
It's okay.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:37.580
Anyway, why did you stay home from school?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.460
I wanted to get ready for things.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:45.240
There's this new stuff, 
the coins and key cards.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.470
Get ready to fight?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.310
If you lose this time, 
you lose your memories, right?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.390
There are lots of memories 
I don't want to lose.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.650
Hitoe...

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
What are you doing after school?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
There's someplace I want to stop by.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
Does it have to do with the Selector battles?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
Yes.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
What happened?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.230
Nothing, I just want to look into some things.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.360
I want to help. 
Tell me if something happens.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.950
I want to help. 
Tell me if something happens. 

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.610
Piruluk.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:10.200
What?

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.550
We're starting with three 
coins this time, right?

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:16.380
Yeah.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:17.870
Everyone starts with three.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.090
Do these coins include the 
memories I lost last time?

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:27.930
No. These coins are your memories, 
split into five parts.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:32.590
But if you win all the battles, 
you can alter one of your memories.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:36.100
You should be able to recover 
your lost memories that way.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.350
And the key card, too...

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.820
The basic rules of the 
battles haven't changed,

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.900
but this new element allows you 
to change your coin skill.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.580
Change it?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.890
I don't know what will happen...

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.120
But I think these cards will 
determine the winner.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.500
So I'll need to test how 
they work in a battle?

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.200
I'm sorry.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.470
There's no need for you to apologize.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:07.040
Piruluk, I have another wish.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.680
I want to end this cycle of darkness.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.810
Be careful.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:17.900
It feels like there's more to these 
new battles than it looks like.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.800
Practice was extra tough this morning,

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.820
so when I ate lunch, I got really sleepy!

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:25.920
I actually fell half-asleep.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.900
You're not supposed to fall asleep!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.910
But I was half-awake, so it's okay!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.240
Jeez...

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:38.410
<i>Back then, I was the one who fell asleep.</i>

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.270
Chi-chan?

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:41.920
What?

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:46.130
Why did you believe that we 
were childhood friends?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.240
Why...

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:53.600
I just couldn't imagine you lying, maybe?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:07:00.060
And the old me that you tell me 
about really seems like me,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.810
so I think it's probably true.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.320
Someday, I'll remember for real.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.940
When that happens, let's talk 
a bunch about the past.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.900
Yeah.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.090
I'm back.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.660
Tama!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.410
You shouldn't sleep here!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:22.290
Tama-chan was so excited to help 
with the cleaning, she got tired.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.170
Let her sleep until dinnertime.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.430
You're right.

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:27.960
It's so clean now.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.720
Tama's a lot more useful than you are.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.620
What? I'm helping with stuff, too!

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.540
It was true...

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:52.320
Ruuko told me today that the 
Selector battles were continuing.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.820
So Ruuko has an LRIG now, too?

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.960
No, I don't think so.

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:00.630
A girl named Mizushima, who was a Selector,

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:04.490
said that the battles are continuing 
and asked for her help.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.130
But she said she refused.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.620
That's right, thinking about Tama-chan...

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.800
Let's not tell Ruuko.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.680
Yeah, I think that's best.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.140
Anyway, I'll gather information.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.280
Thank you, Yuzuki.

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.900
<i>This is insane.</i>

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.490
<i>We went through of all that to end this.</i>

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.360
<i>So why did it come back?</i>

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:39.720
Unproductive.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.900
No useful information gained.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.980
Why not give up and fight a battle instead?

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:46.580
Refusal.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.670
I have some free time today. 
I'll head over there.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.180
<b>We Have
Battle Tables</b>

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:56.050
Oh, welcome, Hanna-san.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:57.410
It's been a while.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.260
Hello, Kurebayashi-san.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.130
It's rare for you to come to Shinjuku, isn't it?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:02.980
Research.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:05.580
I heard a rumor I could use for a column.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.690
Have you heard anything about it?

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.220
What rumor?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.340
Question.

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:12.970
Have you ever heard of Selector battles?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.650
Affirmation? You have?

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:18.690
No, I haven't.

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:20.660
Some kind of new card game?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.740
Hearsay.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.120
I've heard a rumor

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:30.720
that there's a special kind of WIXOSS 
battle held by the chosen.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.100
And the losers forfeit part 
of their memories.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.110
That wasn't the rule...

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.480
Question.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.740
Then what was the rule?

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:40.720
Er, no...

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.330
I mean, that's different from 
the rumor I heard—

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:45.020
Suspicion.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:48.190
Didn't you just tell me you'd heard nothing?

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:52.260
Well, I just remembered.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.620
I heard a similar story...

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.580
But it's just another urban legend, right?

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.450
Distrust. You really think so?

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.950
Hanna-san,

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:08.120
I think it's best not to get 
involved in those things.

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:09.340
Acknowledgment.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.460
Thank you for your concern.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:15.360
But I've already reached a point 
where I can't turn back.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:20.040
If you run across any 
information worth knowing,

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:21.240
contact me.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.640
Yeah. Okay.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.320
Success.

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.770
I met an information source.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.770
But she's not a Selector.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:31.840
Hypothesis.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.650
She's probably a Selector 
from an earlier battle.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.610
You really are smart, Hanna-sama.

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:54.130
Wow, it's so cute!

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:56.100
Oh, man, you're right.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.590
<i>In the Selector battles...</i>

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:06.150
<i>I accomplished nothing.</i>

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:12.440
Akira-chan, can you make a sillier face?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:13.960
Okay!

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:17.540
All the stuff Akira's doing lately is like that.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:17.870
Yeah.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.800
She's turning into a comedy character, right?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.700
Sorry!

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:25.660
You asshole!

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.640
What the hell's your problem?!

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:31.080
I apologized.

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:33.840
This man molested me.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:34.460
Hey!

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:39.720
You want me to end your life just like that?

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:51.580
<i>This scar is all I have left.</i>

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.150
Do you know where the other Selectors are?

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.910
I can sense their general location a little.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.570
I didn't used to be able to...

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.440
They want us to be more 
proactive about battling.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.740
Where are the closest ones around here?

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.460
Let's not do this.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:22.300
Why?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.720
Because this place is...

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.030
Where I fought Satomi.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:29.560
If you can sense a Selector here...

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.130
It might be Carnival, so...

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.940
If I fight, I'll lose?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.920
Satomi was the bookmaker,

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.360
and Carnival was his former LRIG.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.650
She must know a lot.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:46.320
And I need that information.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.290
You don't care what happens to you, do you?

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:54.410
I just want to atone for my sins.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.940
You talk like you're a cold person,

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:01.190
but you were always nice to me.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:07.130
So I'll do whatever I can for you.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:10.850
But I won't help you commit suicide.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.190
All right. Thank you.

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:21.940
Kiyoi, a Selector is coming!

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.340
Hey, you're a Selector, right?

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.680
Let's fight.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:41.750
I'm having a bad day.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.320
Aoi Akira...

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:46.380
Who are you?

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.240
Piruluk.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.510
I was your LRIG.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:52.510
So you were chosen as a Selector again?

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:56.250
Oh, it's you, Piruluk-tan?

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:57.490
I remember you!

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.390
You haven't changed, have you?

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:01.730
Yeah, right...

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.280
Why haven't you changed?!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:07.640
Piruluk, you bitch! Screw you!

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.250
Why am I the only one who 
had to end up like this?!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.230
Everyone used me as a stepping stone!

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.410
You were laughing at me, too, weren't you?!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.560
Right?!

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:20.880
Do it.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.240
You know, don't you?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:28.290
That continuing this will only 
hurt everyone involved.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.890
I don't care! Fight!

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:35.910
I ended up with this face 
because you were weak!

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:38.940
You lost because you 
underestimated Kominato-san—

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.410
Shut up!

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:43.360
It's your fault for being weak! 
Don't try and blame me!

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.820
I only spoke the truth.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:50.780
You used me, right?

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:54.660
Come on, feel some responsibility.

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.660
Feel some responsibility for ruining my life!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.000
That's the way.

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.290
Open!

00:15:19.250 --> 00:15:22.060
So this is what the stage looks like this time?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.520
Let's deal with anything we don't 
understand as we fight.

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:26.840
Together.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:27.610
Right.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:32.640
I always hated that self-satisfied 
look on your face...

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.030
Yahoo!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.080
You're up first, Aki-lucky!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:39.790
I'll make your face twist with pain soon.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:41.130
Grow!

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.220
Summon two Nyphonium.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:44.880
Draw.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:48.170
Magic Hand! Noisy! Star Arrow!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.190
Piruluk!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.050
Combos... That's new.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:57.410
Hang on a minute!

00:15:57.410 --> 00:16:00.500
You're calling your LRIG Piruluk?

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.960
You are creepy that way, aren't you?

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:07.040
Oh, did that hurt you?

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.010
That makes me happy!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:09.800
Grow.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:11.890
Summon Manomin.

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:13.410
Discard hand and attack.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.860
You still like tossing away cards, huh?

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:23.580
I guess you're too stupid to 
learn more than one trick.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.540
And you're still trying to provoke 
and distract me, aren't you?

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:28.840
What?

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:32.780
I'm not trying to provoke you. 
I'm trying to help you out.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:35.890
Keep doing the same thing 
over and over, and you'll lose.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.990
Grow.

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:40.180
Black?

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:43.770
When I was with you, Piruluk-tan, 
I used a blue deck, right?

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:47.400
But this one suits me better now.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.970
Bloody Out!

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:51.970
Piruluk!

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:56.110
Aki-lucky, want to follow up 
with another attack?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.870
Nope. Turn end.

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:01.170
Akira's fighting style has changed, as well.

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:04.040
Before, she just used brute strength.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:05.960
What do we do?

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.030
Coin bet.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.380
Peeping.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:14.880
Okay, me, too.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.210
Coin bet.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:22.640
I can't tell...

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:28.060
You're panicking, aren't you, Piruluk-tan?

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.100
But you can't help it!

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:32.820
Happening!

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:37.150
Happening is a coin skill whose 
effects can't be predicted.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:39.030
There's no way to tell what it'll do.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.650
Oh? That's what it did this time...

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.820
Ironic!

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:48.260
Your favorite tactic's come 
back to haunt you!

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.660
Hey, you okay?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:02.740
If I'm strong when I pair up 
with an LRIG who's not you,

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:06.570
that means you're useless!

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.340
It's because I'm so smart, isn't it?

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:11.910
Shut up!

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:15.540
If you interrupt me with your crap 
when I'm talking, I'll rip you in half!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.570
Aki-lucky, you're scary!

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:22.080
Piruluk!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.840
It's okay.

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.200
I can still fight.

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.460
Akira really is strong.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:31.540
Kiyoi, there's something 
we haven't tried yet.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:39.250
Piruluk, tell me how to use my key card.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.280
Okay.

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.550
Say "Unlock" and bet a coin.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.100
Unlock.

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:46.790
Coin bet.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:05.200
What is that?

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.830
I... I don't know!

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:15.740
What's this?

00:19:19.150 --> 00:19:20.860
Let's go, Kiyoi.

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:24.760
Coin bet.

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.060
Catharsis!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.930
What the hell was that?!

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:41.400
Huh? Whawhawhat?

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:51.160
This time, if you lose a battle, 
you lose your LRIG, huh?

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.040
So it seems.

00:19:53.360 --> 00:19:55.360
What the hell did you just do?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.710
Give her back, damn it!

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:00.800
What is this?

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.800
Screw you!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.680
Piruluk, you bitch!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:08.330
It's true that I used you, once.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.680
I can understand why you'd hate me.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:13.520
But I have a responsibility to 
end the Selector battles.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:13.520
I don't care!

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.700
I'm going to beat the shit out of you

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:20.940
and make your face twist with despair!

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:32.570
It's been a while, little bitch.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:34.980
Carnival...

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:36.220
Yes.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.720
I hope you can keep calling me that.

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:41.460
I did like Kou,

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:45.260
but I don't like using the name 
of someone who failed.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.470
Failed?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:51.780
He lost the battles, and now he 
can't have any more fun, right?

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:54.840
I plan to keep the battles going forever

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.990
and enjoy them for eternity.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:59.960
Enjoy... this?

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.380
This world is so boring.

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:03.990
But that is different.

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:07.300
Little bitch, you know 
what I'm talking about.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.720
You were having fun, even if 
you wouldn't admit it, right?

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.350
Your battle with Aoi Akira.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:17.800
Now, let us begin a battle where the 
weak are devoured by the strong!

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:19.270
How exciting!

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:21.800
I can hear the screams of girls 
begging for their lives again!

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.760
Very well.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.230
Let us begin.

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:28.840
But I won't let you have your way.

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:34.770
This time, I will put a stop 
to these Selector battles

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.500
and this endless cycle of despair!

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:38.900
Sounds fun.

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:40.540
Try it.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:44.990
Initiation / Usual and Unusual

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:25.520
Riru?

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:27.680
Hello again, Suzuko.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.080
You're so nice, Riru.

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:30.420
The Selectors become LRIGs?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:32.040
There's still too much we don't understand.

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:32.780
Kanae-san!

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:34.640
If you lose, your opponent steals your LRIG.

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:38.260
Another new Selector has been chosen.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:40.980
Crowding / Loser and Winner

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:40.760
Crowding / Loser and Winner.
